PTF RPM Repository Automation & Fleet Delivery
SUSE MULTI-LINUX MANAGER (MLM) STANDARD OPERATING PROCEDURE
Problem Statement & Solution Summary:
SUSE Multi-Linux Manager (MLM) currently lacks a native, built-in mechanism to directly import, index, and
distribute vendor Program Temporary Fixes (PTFs) for Multi Linux Support Minions into channels. This
operational limitation creates manual friction and delay when hotfixes must be urgently rolled out across
large enterprise environments.
What This Solution Provides: An automated, enterprise-ready ingestion pipeline consisting of: (1) an interactive,
secure credentialed PTF batch downloader; (2) an automated filesystem watcher with 120-second quiet-window
debouncing; (3) automatic Yum/RPM repository index regeneration ( createrepo_c ); (4) automated MLM channel
synchronization ( spacewalk-repo-sync ); and (5) targeted Salt orchestration with zero-rebuild CLM injection to
safely deploy fixes to 1,000+ RHEL 7 / MLS 7 systems without service interruption.
