7. Fleet-Wide Deployment to 1,000+ MLS 7 / RHEL 7 Minions
Option A: Direct System Group Assignment (Standard Fleet)
1. In the MLM Web UI, subscribe the MLS7-Fleet system group to the child channel custom-ptf
mls7_ltss-x86_64 .
2. Trigger fleet installation via the MLM Salt master (leveraging native yum on the minions):
mgrctl exec -- salt -G 'systemgroup:MLS7-Fleet' pkg.install <ptf-package-name> # Or direct command-line
execution:
mgrctl exec -- salt -G 'systemgroup:MLS7-Fleet' cmd.run "yum clean expire-cache && yum install -y
<ptf-package-name>"
Option B: Zero-Rebuild Injection into Frozen CLM Environments
Zero-Rebuild Workflow: Prevents full CLM project rebuilds by injecting verified PTF packages directly into the
active frozen clone channels.
1. Identify the target environment channel label:
spacecmd -u admin -p <PWD> -- softwarechannel_list | grep "clm-.*-custom-ptf"
2. Inject the RPM directly into the target CLM clone:
spacecmd -u admin -p <PWD> -- softwarechannel_addpackages <CLM_TARGET_CHANNEL> "<ptf
package-name>*"
3. Trigger immediate client update across the fleet:
mgrctl exec -- salt -G 'systemgroup:MLS7-Fleet' cmd.run "yum clean expire-cache && yum install -y
<ptf-package-name>"
